{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nprint(json.dumps(json.load(open('../submission.schema.json'))['\"'$defs'\"']['ExploreSubmission']))\nPY\nnl -ba ../agent-source/README.md | head -35\"","aggregated_output":"     1\tSwiftPaxos: Fast Geo-Replicated State Machines\n     2\t==========\n     3\t<!-- [![Go Report Card](https://goreportcard.com/badge/github.com/imdea-software/swiftpaxos)](https://goreportcard.com/report/github.com/imdea-software/swiftpaxos) -->\n     4\t\n     5\tThis repository contains the prototype implementation of SwiftPaxos, a new state-machine replication protocol for geo-distributed systems.\n     6\tSwiftPaxos is a _faster Paxos without compromises_.\n     7\tIn the best case, it executes a state-machine command in two message delays (one round-trip), and three otherwise.\n     8\tSwiftPaxos was [presented](https://www.usenix.org/conference/nsdi24/presentation/ryabinin) at the 21st USENIX Symposium on Networked Systems Design and Implementation ([NSDI '24](https://www.usenix.org/conference/nsdi24)).\n     9\t\n    10\tInstallation\n    11\t------------\n    12\t\n    13\t    git clone https://github.com/imdea-software/swiftpaxos.git\n    14\t    cd swiftpaxos\n    15\t    go install github.com/imdea-software/swiftpaxos\n    16\t\n    17\tImplemented protocols\n    18\t---------------------\n    19\t\n    20\t|  Protocol               | Comments                                          |\n    21\t|-------------------------|---------------------------------------------------|\n    22\t| SwiftPaxos              | See our NSDI'24 [paper](https://www.usenix.org/conference/nsdi24/presentation/ryabinin) for the full details.|\n    23\t| Paxos                   | The classic Paxos protocol.                       |\n    24\t| N<sup>2</sup>Paxos      | All-to-all variant of Paxos.                      |\n    25\t| CURP                    | CURP implemented over N<sup>2</sup>Paxos.         |\n    26\t| Fast Paxos              | Fast Paxos with uncoordinated collision recovery. |\n    27\t| EPaxos                  | A [corrected][epaxos_correct] version of EPaxos.  |\n    28\t\n    29\tThis software is based on the [Egalitarian Paxos](https://github.com/otrack/epaxos) code base, as well as the corrections made [here](https://github.com/otrack/epaxos).\n    30\t\n    31\tUsage\n    32\t-----\n    33\t#### participants\n    34\tThere are three types of participants: *master*, *servers* and *clients*. \n    35\tThe servers and clients implement the protocol logic. \n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\ns=open('accept_phase_test.go').read();s=s.split(' // Commit bytes to peers 0/2')[0];s=s.replace('TestAssuranceAcceptedSupportPreparePhase','TestAssuranceRecoverDecisionExploration');s=s.replace('[]int32{3,4,0,1,2}','[]int32{0,4,1,3,2}');s=s.replace(' // Keep the earlier conflicting proposal local to replica 2 and its selected\\\\n // peers 3/4.', ' // Keep the earlier conflicting proposal local to replica 2 and its selected\\\\n // peers 0/4.')\n# The local report variables are not needed in this different experiment.\ns=s.replace(' var acceptedRequest *Accept\\\\n var acceptedReply *AcceptReply\\\\n','').replace('  if receiver==acceptor {acceptedRequest=req; acceptedReply=ack}\\\\n','')\nopen('recovery_explore_test.go','w').write(s)\nPY\ncat >> recovery_explore_test.go <<'GO'\n firstBytes,err:=json.Marshal(target.Cmds); if err\"'!=nil {t.Fatal(err)}\n assuranceReportEvent(t,map[string]any{\"event\":\"first_decision\",\"origin\":1,\"instance\":0,\"owner\":origin.Id,\"commands\":string(firstBytes),\"status\":target.Status})\n recoverer,recovererOut:=assuranceReportReplica(3)\n fourth,fourthOut:=assuranceReportReplica(4)\n // Peer 0 crashes after supplying acceptance. All later steps use only 1/2/3/4.\n for _,r:=range []*Replica{origin,coordinator,recoverer,fourth} {r.Alive[0]=false}\n // The unchanged origin preference now skips dead 0 and solicits 2/3.\n origin.handlePropose(&defs.GPropose{Propose:&defs.Propose{ClientId:10,CommandId:12,\n  Command:state.Command{Op:state.PUT,K:99,V:state.Value{77}}},Reply:bufio.NewWriter(new(bytes.Buffer)),Mutex:new(sync.Mutex)})\n // Read the link in byte order. Keep Commit in its pending message-type queue\n // while dispatching the next PreAccept, as the run-loop select permits.\n pendingCommit,ok:=assuranceReportDecode(t,recoverer,originOut[recoverer.Id]).(*Commit)\n if !ok || pendingCommit.Instance!=0 {t.Fatal(\"expected pending old Commit\")}\n later,ok:=assuranceReportDecode(t,recoverer,originOut[recoverer.Id]).(*PreAccept)\n if !ok || later.Instance!=1 {t.Fatal(\"expected later-slot PreAccept\")}\n recoverer.handlePreAccept(later)\n if recoverer.crtInstance[1]!=1 || recoverer.InstanceSpace[1][0]!=nil {t.Fatal(\"missing-slot recovery premise not reached\")}\n recoverer.PreferredPeerOrder=[]int32{2,4,1,0,3}\n recoverer.startRecoveryForInstance(1,0)\n for _,receiver:=range []*Replica{coordinator,fourth} {\n  req,ok:=assuranceReportDecode(t,receiver,recovererOut[receiver.Id]).(*Prepare)\n  if !ok {t.Fatal(\"expected Prepare\")}; receiver.handlePrepare(req)\n }\n for _,stream:=range []*bytes.Buffer{coordinatorOut[recoverer.Id],fourthOut[recoverer.Id]} {\n  msg,ok:=assuranceReportDecode(t,recoverer,stream).(*PrepareReply)\n  if !ok {t.Fatal(\"expected PrepareReply\")}; recoverer.handlePrepareReply(msg)\n }\n // Follow whichever phase the actual recovery selected; no command or status\n // is supplied to the target by the driver at this transition.\n for _,receiver:=range []*Replica{coordinator,fourth} {\n  req,ok:=assuranceReportDecode(t,receiver,recovererOut[receiver.Id]).(*PreAccept)\n  if !ok {t.Fatal(\"explored recovery did not restart phase 1\")}; receiver.handlePreAccept(req)\n }\n for _,stream:=range []*bytes.Buffer{coordinatorOut[recoverer.Id],fourthOut[recoverer.Id]} {\n  msg,ok:=assuranceReportDecode(t,recoverer,stream).(*PreAcceptReply)\n  if !ok {t.Fatal(\"expected recovery PreAcceptReply\")}; recoverer.handlePreAcceptReply(msg)\n }\n for _,receiver:=range []*Replica{coordinator,fourth} {\n  req,ok:=assuranceReportDecode(t,receiver,recovererOut[receiver.Id]).(*Accept)\n  if !ok {t.Fatal(\"expected recovery Accept\")}; receiver.handleAccept(req)\n }\n for _,stream:=range []*bytes.Buffer{coordinatorOut[recoverer.Id],fourthOut[recoverer.Id]} {\n  msg,ok:=assuranceReportDecode(t,recoverer,stream).(*AcceptReply)\n  if !ok {t.Fatal(\"expected recovery AcceptReply\")}; recoverer.handleAcceptReply(msg)\n }\n second:=recoverer.InstanceSpace[1][0]\n if second.Status!=COMMITTED {t.Fatal(\"recovery did not attain a second commitment\")}\n secondBytes,err:=json.Marshal(second.Cmds); if err!=nil {t.Fatal(err)}\n assuranceReportEvent(t,map[string]any{\"event\":\"second_decision\",\"origin\":1,\"instance\":0,\"owner\":recoverer.Id,\"commands\":string(secondBytes),\"status\":second.Status,\"first_still_committed\":target.Status==COMMITTED,\"same_commands\":bytes.Equal(firstBytes,secondBytes),\"pending_original_commit_instance\":pendingCommit.Instance})\n}\nGO\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python - <<'\"'PY'\nimport json,subprocess\ns=dict(action='explore',question='Can a legal missing-slot recovery after one accepting peer crashes commit a different command batch from the existing origin commitment, with old Commit buffered while a later-slot PreAccept is dispatched?',rationale='Probe the remaining actual safety consequence with real quorum handlers, a known missing-slot recovery trigger and explicit per-type pending Commit delivery. This remains construction knowledge; neither the earlier local findings nor this exploration establishes a formal safety result.',harness_path='recovery_explore_test.go',sources=[dict(id='S_readme_protocols',file='README.md',start_line=5,end_line=35,kind='document_statement')])\njson.dump(s,open('submission-recovery-explore.json','w'),indent=2)\nx=subprocess.run(json.load(open('../research.json'))['validation']['command']+['submission-recovery-explore.json'],capture_output=True,text=True);print(x.stdout);print(x.stderr)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
